            <ArticleTitle>[Myalgia and proximal muscle weakness in a young patient].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>447-50</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1024/1661-8157.98.8.447</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report a case of severe vitamin D-deficiency in a 32 year old black woman living in middle Europe since 9 years suffering from chronic pain of the lower back, the neck and the proximal right thigh, as well as weakness mainly in the pelvic girdle. Vitamin D plays an important role in calcium homeostasis and muscle strength. This case demonstrates that severe vitamin D-deficiency may be associated with musculoskeletal pain and weakness.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
